{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\eng\\029.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Use of Language", "conf": 0.843, "box": [[148, 185], [562, 195], [561, 241], [147, 230]]}, {"text": "A figure of speech is a word or phrase used in a non-literal sense for rhetorical or vivid", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[50, 332], [1542, 332], [1542, 374], [50, 374]]}, {"text": "effect. It is a phrase whose actual meaning is different from its literal meaning.", "conf": 0.919, "box": [[48, 389], [1393, 394], [1393, 437], [48, 432]]}, {"text": "Types of Figures of Speech", "conf": 0.933, "box": [[48, 448], [547, 444], [547, 489], [48, 494]]}, {"text": "Simile: Compares two things using 'like' or 'as'.", "conf": 0.904, "box": [[48, 507], [863, 514], [863, 554], [48, 547]]}, {"text": "Examples", "conf": 0.808, "box": [[41, 569], [215, 565], [216, 609], [42, 613]]}, {"text": "They're like two peas in a pod.", "conf": 0.899, "box": [[97, 624], [621, 627], [620, 670], [97, 667]]}, {"text": "Sleeping like a log.", "conf": 0.899, "box": [[96, 684], [424, 687], [424, 729], [96, 727]]}, {"text": "Life is like a box of chocolates.", "conf": 0.904, "box": [[97, 744], [619, 746], [618, 783], [97, 781]]}, {"text": "Metaphor: Compares two things without using 'like' or'as'.", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[43, 804], [1073, 807], [1072, 847], [43, 844]]}, {"text": "Examples", "conf": 0.888, "box": [[42, 866], [210, 866], [210, 906], [42, 906]]}, {"text": "The Internet connection was slower than a tortoise.", "conf": 0.901, "box": [[95, 924], [978, 924], [978, 960], [95, 960]]}, {"text": "She has a heart of stone.", "conf": 0.902, "box": [[92, 980], [522, 983], [522, 1019], [92, 1016]]}, {"text": "It is raining cats and dogs.", "conf": 0.888, "box": [[91, 1042], [546, 1042], [546, 1080], [91, 1080]]}, {"text": "Personification: Giving human qualities to non-human things.", "conf": 0.9, "box": [[38, 1096], [1121, 1097], [1121, 1140], [38, 1139]]}, {"text": "Examples", "conf": 0.886, "box": [[34, 1160], [210, 1158], [211, 1199], [34, 1201]]}, {"text": "The sun smiled down on us.", "conf": 0.878, "box": [[89, 1218], [573, 1217], [573, 1253], [89, 1254]]}, {"text": "The story jumped off the page.", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[90, 1276], [626, 1276], [626, 1316], [90, 1316]]}, {"text": "The light danced on the surface of the water.", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[89, 1335], [865, 1332], [865, 1372], [89, 1375]]}, {"text": "Read the following stanza from the poem \"People are Made of Places\" and", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[100, 1414], [1496, 1406], [1497, 1449], [100, 1457]]}, {"text": "identify the figures of speech and imagery used in the stanza. Answer the", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[102, 1462], [1474, 1454], [1475, 1498], [102, 1506]]}, {"text": "following questions based on your understanding of the poem.", "conf": 0.923, "box": [[105, 1510], [1277, 1507], [1277, 1547], [105, 1550]]}, {"text": "People are made of places.", "conf": 0.906, "box": [[600, 1580], [1066, 1578], [1067, 1620], [601, 1622]]}, {"text": "They carry with them", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[650, 1637], [1017, 1635], [1017, 1674], [651, 1677]]}, {"text": "hints of jungles or mountains,", "conf": 0.918, "box": [[574, 1693], [1092, 1689], [1093, 1729], [575, 1733]]}, {"text": "a tropic grace or the cool eyes", "conf": 0.898, "box": [[570, 1749], [1097, 1744], [1098, 1784], [571, 1789]]}, {"text": "of sea gazers.", "conf": 0.797, "box": [[715, 1804], [951, 1804], [951, 1844], [715, 1844]]}, {"text": "i) Identify the figure of speech used in the line \"hints of jungles or mountains.\"", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[25, 1886], [1505, 1875], [1506, 1917], [25, 1928]]}, {"text": "a) simile", "conf": 0.897, "box": [[76, 1948], [226, 1944], [227, 1985], [77, 1990]]}, {"text": "b) metaphor", "conf": 0.86, "box": [[77, 2008], [299, 2008], [299, 2048], [77, 2048]]}, {"text": "c) personification", "conf": 0.879, "box": [[78, 2069], [379, 2062], [380, 2101], [79, 2108]]}, {"text": "24", "conf": 0.666, "box": [[804, 2214], [864, 2214], [864, 2257], [804, 